WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.740
From creepy-crawly parasites to sci-fi space
mutinies, some movie scenes are so shocking

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.180
that they stick with you for the rest of the
week — or the rest of your life.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.790
But if you need help remembering the unforgettable,
here's an eyeball-searing, gut-punching roundup

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.810
of all those disturbing Hollywood moments
that audiences never saw coming.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.860
And in case it's not obvious, here's your
final warning that this video contains spoilers

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.020
for an awful lot of movies.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:24.880
"Hold onto your butts."

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.740
Bursting out

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:32.390
With its dripping mouth and phallic head,
the xenomorph from Alien is pure nightmare

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.390
fuel.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:36.460
But if you're looking for something that'll
scar you for life, then it doesn't get any

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.420
worse than this explosive scene.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.010
It all starts when executive officer Kane,
played by John Hurt, winds up in a coma with

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:47.460
an extraterrestrial creature attached to his
head — then wakes up, only to develop the

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.420
worst case of heartburn in history.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:55.329
When his comrades lay him down on the table,
Kane's chest blows apart, revealing… well,

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:55.840
this guy.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:02.800
Naturally, the rest of the crew are completely
freaked out— as were audiences, who thought

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.310
Kane was out of danger when the facehugger
fell off, and who were definitely not expecting

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:12.200
a demonic worm to burst out of his thorax
mere minutes later.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.899
Mind-control eels

00:01:13.899 --> 00:01:18.959
Star Trek was a story about unity, harmony,
and working together for the good of mankind

00:01:18.959 --> 00:01:21.719
— that is, until The Wrath of Khan came
along.

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:26.899
Then, it was a story about unity and harmony,
but also about freaky horrible parasites that

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:30.880
crawl through your ear, into your brain, and
turn you into a mindless slave.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.579
The Ceti eel is a favorite weapon of Khan
Noonien Singh a genetically enhanced superhuman

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:40.689
who wants revenge against Captain Kirk for
abandoning him on an inhospitable planet.

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:45.770
As part of his plan, Khan uses the eel to
force Starfleet's Terrell and Chekov to tell

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:49.819
him everything they know — leading to this
terrifying sequence in which the disgusting

00:01:49.819 --> 00:01:55.479
creature inches its way into the screaming
Chekov's ear canal.

00:01:55.479 --> 00:01:56.950
Buried alive

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.109
This slow-burner of a suspense film spends
a long time leading up to one of the freakiest

00:02:01.109 --> 00:02:06.539
finales in history — one so disturbing that
Bravo ranked it as the 55th scariest movie

00:02:06.539 --> 00:02:07.630
scene of all time.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:11.900
The Vanishing centers on a man named Rex,
whose girlfriend Saskia disappeared three

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.590
years ago without a trace.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:18.640
Rex knows that Saskia is almost certainly
a goner, but he's desperate to unravel the

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.930
mystery of her disappearance — which leads
him to make an incredibly stupid bargain with

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.340
the man who kidnapped her.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:28.120
If Rex wants to know the truth about what
happened to her, he'll have to experience

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.689
her fate firsthand.

00:02:29.689 --> 00:02:34.170
Driven by insatiable curiosity, Rex agrees
and downs a sleeping pill.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:38.620
When he wakes up, he's been buried alive…
and he's really not happy about it.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:45.340
You've gotta hand it to The Vanishing for
managing to pull off this shocking ending

00:02:45.359 --> 00:02:48.349
after more than ninety minutes of ominous
foreshadowing.

00:02:48.349 --> 00:02:53.200
We knew something bad was going to happen,
but nobody expected it to be that bad.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.200
The final confession

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:58.690
A few years before starting a fight club,
Edward Norton made his feature film debut

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:04.709
in Primal Fear as Aaron Stampler, a troubled
altar boy accused of ending the life of an

00:03:04.709 --> 00:03:05.709
archbishop.

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:09.340
The high-profile case draws the attention
of Martin Vail, a smarmy lawyer played by

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:14.610
Richard Gere, who uncovers a shocking truth:
after years of abuse by the archbishop, Aaron

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:19.980
developed a second personality—a violent
and dangerous man who calls himself Roy.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.700
After Roy confesses to the homicide, Vail
uses his expert legal skills to save the young

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.420
man's life and have him committed to a mental
institution.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:32.639
But in the final moments of the film, the
truth is revealed: the split personality scheme

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:33.920
was one big hoax.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.120
"There never was a Roy."

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:39.709
"There never was an Aaron."

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:40.709
Surprise!

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:46.560
Sweet, simple Aaron was all an act, while
the sociopathic Roy was the real deal the

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.900
entire time.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.599
And now he's gotten away with the crime of
the century!

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:56.690
When Richard Gere walks away stunned, everyone
watching felt the exact same way.

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.499
Keeping it in the family

00:03:58.499 --> 00:04:03.939
There are twist endings, and then there are
twisted endings, and boy, does Oldboy have

00:04:03.939 --> 00:04:04.939
a doozy.

00:04:04.939 --> 00:04:10.120
In this Korean thriller, a man named Oh Dae-su
sets out to get revenge on the man who put

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:12.069
him in prison for fifteen years.

00:04:12.069 --> 00:04:17.049
But during his hunt, he meets up with a young
woman named Mi-do and the two soon become

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:18.419
lovers.

00:04:18.419 --> 00:04:23.500
Imagine Oh Dae-su's horror when he realizes
that it was all a setup by his old enemy,

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:28.419
and the woman he just slept with is actually
the daughter he hasn't seen in fifteen years—

00:04:28.419 --> 00:04:34.280
and also imagine the audience's horror when
Oh Dae-su tries to atone for his sins by cutting

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:36.870
off his own tongue with a pair of scissors.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:41.370
With that moment of graphic violence followed
by an uncomfortably ambiguous ending, it's

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:46.020
no surprise that people still consider Oldboy
to be one of the world's most disturbing viewing

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.380
experiences.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:48.980
Body swap

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:54.760
When she accepts a job working as a caregiver
at a creepy plantation home in 2005's Skeleton

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:58.660
Key, Caroline quickly realizes that there's
something a little off about the elderly couple

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:02.220
who live there — particularly Violet, the
lady of the house.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:05.780
What she doesn't know — and neither does
the audience — is that her amateur detective

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:11.680
work into a world of black magic and ancient
conspiracies is about to backfire horribly.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:16.921
Violet is actually a centuries-old hoodoo
practitioner named Mama Cecile, and Caroline

00:05:16.921 --> 00:05:21.199
plays right into her hands when she traps
herself inside a magical circle that allows

00:05:21.199 --> 00:05:23.470
Mama Cecile to steal her body.

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:27.840
With the help of a menacing mirror, Mama Cecile
performs a sort of swap, taking control of

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:33.710
Caroline's physical form and trapping Caroline
inside Violet's dying, old frame… forever.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:37.750
Unlike many horror films, there's no last-minute
intervention in which the heroine saves the

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:38.750
day.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:43.100
Caroline is simply doomed to spend the rest
of her days as an eighty year-old woman — and

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:48.220
considering how old her new body is, she won't
have many days left.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.900
Assault and revenge

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:54.910
In a movie full of mysterious disappearances,
violent misogyny, and dismembered cats, there's

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:59.699
still one moment that stands out as particularly
shocking in The Girl with the Dragon tattoo.

00:05:59.699 --> 00:06:04.251
It comes early on, when Lisbeth Salander,
played by Rooney Mara, goes to meet her new

00:06:04.251 --> 00:06:09.130
guardian — a sadistic monster who cuffs
her to a bed and violently assaults her.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:14.510
The scene is one of the most sickening ever
depicted on film, and… well, do we need

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.750
to say more?

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.419
"That won't be necessary."

00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:22.270
Some films might wind down from there, but
this one just ups the ante: Lisbeth returns

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:26.960
to her attacker's apartment with a few tools
of revenge — including a tattoo gun that

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:30.950
she uses to leave a nice little message across
her tormentor's torso.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:35.620
As satisfying as it is to see Lisbeth get
justice, this sequence and its predecessor

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.670
are hard to watch.

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:38.670
Batting practice

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:44.009
The gritty, grimy Texas-noir film Cold in
July centers on a trio of men who are on a

00:06:44.009 --> 00:06:48.690
quest to uncover the true identity of a mystery
man named Freddy Russell — and at first,

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:51.000
it seems like your typical conspiracy thriller.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.259
The big twist comes when our heroes begin
to suspect that Freddy is a federal informant

00:06:55.259 --> 00:07:00.140
and set out to meet him, only to discover
a stash of VHS tapes that turn out to be snuff

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.140
films.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:05.360
The movie doesn't make us watch Freddy beating
his victims with a baseball bat, but we see

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:10.280
Michael C. Hall and Don Johnson see it, which
along with some strategic sound work is more

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.090
than enough to convey the horror.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:16.009
It's also one of the hardest left turns in
thriller history, one that gives our three

00:07:16.009 --> 00:07:21.009
heroes a new purpose and recasts the entire
movie in a whole new light.

00:07:21.009 --> 00:07:22.699
What's on the menu?

00:07:22.699 --> 00:07:27.460
Snowpiercer doesn't scrimp on disturbing material,
particularly when it comes to food.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:31.620
The first big gross-out comes when Curtis,
played by Chris Evans, finds out just what's

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:36.360
in those greasy, gelatinous protein blocks
he and his friends have been eating for years.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:39.480
(more bugs than Assassin's Creed Unity)

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:46.540
But even then, munching on bugs is a lot better
than eating people — which brings us to

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.580
the second big shock in this film.

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:52.689
Curtis reveals that when he first boarded
the train years ago, there was no food in

00:07:52.689 --> 00:07:56.110
the tail section, leading many to resort to
cannibalism.

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:57.340
But that's not all:

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:01.180
"I know that babies taste best."

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:06.860
In addition to being a shocking revelation,
this moment is a brilliant subversion of Chris

00:08:06.860 --> 00:08:08.930
Evans' most famous role.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:15.110
After "babies taste best", will you ever look
at Captain America the same way again?

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:16.330
Zara's plunge

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:21.310
When this long-awaited followup to Jurassic
Park hit theaters in 2015, the dino flick

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:26.491
earned over $1 billion worldwide — but it
also left some critics confused, upset, and

00:08:26.491 --> 00:08:30.419
angry, all thanks to one particularly intense
scene.

00:08:30.419 --> 00:08:34.320
Zara is an assistant at Jurassic World who
spends most of her time on the phone, planning

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:39.960
a wedding, and trying to keep tabs on Claire's
unruly nephews… until every monster on the

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:42.380
island decides they want her for dessert.

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:48.270
As all hell breaks loose at the theme park,
Zara is attacked by multiple flying pterosaurs,

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:52.860
one of which toys with her by plunging her
repeatedly into a giant pool of water.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.120
And just when it seems things couldn't get
any worse?

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:02.400
Zara's life comes to a violent, horrifying,
and totally undeserved end.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.700
Even Sam Neill, the star of the original Jurassic
Park, couldn't believe what he was seeing.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.210
In an interview, he asked,

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:10.200
"Boy, what did the English girl do wrong?

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.260
She got eaten by like three dinosaurs at once."

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.870
Good question, Sam.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:15.890
The Ravager mutiny

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:20.940
When it comes to superhero movies, the Marvel
Cinematic Universe is supposed to be upbeat

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:21.940
and fun.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:25.740
But writer-director James Gunn must have missed
that memo when he wrote the Ravager mutiny

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:30.400
scene in the second Guardians of the Galaxy
film, which might just be the most disturbing

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.360
in the history of the MCU.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:38.450
Sick and tired of being bossed around by Yondu,
this incredibly ugly alien named Taserface

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:42.660
leads a Ravager mutiny, deposing the captain
and taking control of the ship.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:47.030
Naturally, not everyone is cool with the coup,
but Taserface isn't much for talking things

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:49.040
out and reaching a peaceful compromise.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:54.360
Instead, he summarily executes anyone who's
still loyal to Yondu, tossing them into space

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:58.570
where they succumb to the freezing, airless
climate in a matter of seconds.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:02.660
Even though it ends up being a visual foreshadowing
of one of the movie's coolest scenes, in which

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:06.960
a bunch of hovering Ravager ships light up
for Yondu's funeral, the haunting image of

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:11.830
all those frozen corpses floating through
space is horrifying and not easily forgotten

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:16.530
— even if Rocket does give old Taserface
the mocking he richly deserves.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.220
"What was your second choice?

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:20.080
Sack hat?"

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:26.030
Ultimately, the Ravager mutiny was such a
dark scene that it left some viewers with

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:29.270
mixed feelings about the Guardians' second
big-screen outing.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:34.260
But thankfully, the crowd-pleasing David Hasselhoff
cameos are enough to satisfy most fans that

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:37.450
this fun-loving franchise hasn't lost its
way.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:38.450
Thanks for watching!

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.210
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:43.200
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

